-- Fact 3 of whole-program specialisation (`backend.md` §9) when a record
-- escapes in a unit the worklist walks before a function that spreads it
-- (`{ r | a = … }`), in the same sweep: the escape makes every key of the
-- record one the program cannot see written, and the spread must copy that
-- to the new record. Walked by the worklist, the spreading body never saw
-- it, and a safety build's comparison with a sweep of everything panicked.
-- Both builds print the key the host added.
import Node
import Probe


main : Node.Program
main = Node.printLines (Probe.demo ⊤)
